Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Omadungeon
Upstream-Contact: ferreo <ferreo@pika-os.com>
Source: https://github.com/ferrreo/omadungeon
Comment:
 The binary packages ship a single self-contained Godot export with the game's
 PCK embedded in the executable, so most files listed below are present inside
 /usr/lib/omadungeon/omadungeon even though they are not visible as separate
 paths on disk. The exceptions are the paths named in the export presets'
 exclude_filter - addons/, tests/, tools/, docs/ and the build scripts - which
 are part of the source but are not packed into either binary; the stanzas
 below say so where it matters. The bundled Omarchy Radio tracks are the only
 component that is not distributed under a free licence; see the
 "Files: assets/music/radio/*" stanza and /usr/share/doc/omadungeon/CREDITS.md.
Files-Excluded:
 .godot/*
 export/*

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 ferrreo
License: BSD-3-Clause
Comment:
 Covers the game code (src/, tests/, tools/, data/), the procedurally
 generated pixel art in assets/sprites/, assets/tiles/ and assets/music/
 fallback loops, the sound effects in assets/sfx/ (generated in-house by
 tools/gen-sfx.py), the packaging in packaging/ and this Debian packaging.
 It does not cover addons/, which is third party; see the stanza below.

Files: addons/gdUnit4/*
Copyright: 2023 Mike Schulze
License: MIT
Comment:
 gdUnit4 (https://github.com/MikeSchulze/gdUnit4), the unit-test framework the
 suites in tests/ are written against. It is an editor plugin used only at
 development time: "addons/*" is listed in the exclude_filter of both export
 presets in export_presets.cfg, so no part of it is packed into the exported
 binary and neither binary package distributes it. It is listed here because
 it is present in the source tree. Upstream ships the licence text as
 addons/gdUnit4/LICENSE; it is the same Expat licence quoted below.

Files: debian/*
Copyright: 2026 ferrreo
License: BSD-3-Clause

Files: assets/fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf
Copyright: 2012 The Press Start 2P Project Authors (cody@zone38.net),
           with Reserved Font Name "Press Start 2P"
License: OFL-1.1
Comment: Full text shipped upstream as assets/fonts/OFL-pressstart2p.txt.

Files: assets/fonts/Silkscreen-Regular.ttf
Copyright: 2001 The Silkscreen Project Authors
           (https://github.com/googlefonts/silkscreen), Jason Kottke,
           with Reserved Font Name "Silkscreen"
License: OFL-1.1
Comment: Full text shipped upstream as assets/fonts/OFL-silkscreen.txt.

Files: assets/fonts/VT323-Regular.ttf
Copyright: 2011 The VT323 Project Authors (peter.hull@oikoi.com), Peter Hull,
           with Reserved Font Name "VT323"
License: OFL-1.1
Comment: Full text shipped upstream as assets/fonts/OFL-vt323.txt.

Files: assets/music/radio/*
Copyright: The individual artists credited in docs/CREDITS.md
License: Artist-permission
Comment:
 These are the artist-submitted Omarchy Radio tracks, bundled from
 radio.omarchy.org (upstream repository omacom/radio.omarchy.org). Every track
 and artist is listed in docs/CREDITS.md, installed as
 /usr/share/doc/omadungeon/CREDITS.md and shown on the in-game credits screen.
 Only the omadungeon binary package contains them; omadungeon-lite does not.

