License: Artist-permission
 No licence is stated. The Omarchy Radio upstream repository
 (omacom/radio.omarchy.org) publishes these artist-submitted tracks without a
 licence file and without a copyright assignment, so each track remains the
 property of the individual artist who submitted it, and no free-software
 licence can be claimed for them here.
 .
 They are bundled on the basis of the permission implied by submitting a track
 to a public Omarchy community radio station for use within the Omarchy
 universe. That is an implied permission, not a grant: it does not cover
 relicensing, sale, or redistribution outside that context, and it is not
 DFSG-free. A downstream distributor who is not comfortable with that should
 ship the omadungeon-lite binary package, which contains no Omarchy Radio
 audio at all, or rebuild omadungeon from the "Linux x86_64 (lite, no music)"
 export preset.
 .
 If an artist objects, their track is removed: add the file name to the
 EXCLUDE list at the top of tools/sync-radio.sh and the track is dropped from
 the bundled playlist, from the download set and from docs/CREDITS.md on the
 next sync.
